window.AUD=window.AUD||{};window.AUD.uk=Object.assign(window.AUD.uk||{},{"such as":"","equal to":"","in charge":"","ahead of":"","instead of":"","A fact is true.":"","In this photo essay, we look at pictures and read about festivals, celebrations, and fun events around the world.":"","Children often get money in red paper envelopes.":"","Families light candles and decorate their homes with flowers.":"","Another popular game is volleyball.":"","People watch their favorite players at the World Cup scooter championships.":"","The first team to reach a score of 25 is the winner.":"","Almost every country in the world sends its best athletes to race and play in these games.":"","When a girl turns 15 years old in Mexico, her family and friends often celebrate with food and dancing.":"","This also happens in many parts of Central and South America.":"","A wedding is always a big celebration.":"","In Egypt, dancers and musicians gather around the married couple and dance for up to one hour.":"","People celebrate family reunions all over the world. Aunts, uncles, cousins, and grandparents come together to eat and have fun.":"","Health and Sports Day is an interesting traditional event in Japan.":"","I was surprised, too, because I'm a very good, fast runner.":"","In my village, we always have lots of exciting races and games.":"","My race was very tiring.":"","I am very surprised. I didn't know that about you.":"","Their music is very entertaining. I feel very entertained.":"","It's relaxing to sit in the sun and listen to music. I feel very relaxed.":"","Losing a game is very disappointing. The children are disappointed when they didn't win.":"","We were amazed by the magic.":"","My friends think folk dancing is boring, but I think it is great.":"","We watch traditional plays on Youth and Sports Day.":"","Carlos kicks his red rubber ball so hard.":"","Far across the world, Ashanti is playing Da Ga with her friends.":"","She acts like a snake and tries to tag the next Da Ga.":"","She bounces the ball as hard as she can.":"","It flies over a forest, white cliffs, and a blue ocean.":"","Hyo plays with little dark pebbles.":"","Hyo is finding the perfect place to put his stone.":"","It flies far into the sky, over plains and seas.":"","Matias tosses a stone, and Maria jumps over it.":"","She lands in the next box without stepping on the line.":"","She puts her arms out to keep her balance.":"","The whole family watches as the ball goes up and up until they can't see it anymore.":"","The ball flies over lakes, canyons, and streams.":"","A popular children's game in Mexico is The Blind Hen.":"","You start by choosing one child to be the hen and covering their eyes so that they can't see.":"","The next step is covering the child's eyes.":"","Underline the words ending in -ing.":"","I prefer playing ball games.":"","A preview helps you know what will happen next.":"","Moving is hard work.":"","Mom and I are still unpacking boxes.":"","She and I were packing them just eight weeks ago.":"","It's very quiet compared to Mumbai.":"","The weather in July is warm and sunny.":"","Meeting neighbors isn't easy for me.":"","Dad started his new job as a surgeon at the hospital.":"","I threw snowballs.":"","Please write soon!":"","I rake leaves every Saturday in our yard.":"","Emily is my neighbor and my classmate.":"","Emily, Ashli, and Rachel are coming over on Sunday to work on our science project.":"","What is the order of events?":"","In those days, lots of people could crochet, knit, and sew.":"","We use \"can\" and \"could\" to talk about ability.":"","My grandma gave me knitting lessons.":"","Moving from here to there!":"","People move from rural areas to urban areas, such as cities, to get a job.":"","Everyday people pack their belongings and move to new places.":"","Maybe they came from a rural area, or from a nearby city or town.":"","Perhaps they came from another country.":"","In 1990, about a quarter of the people in China lived in cities.":"","Today, over half of the Chinese people live in cities.":"","Immigrants from Europe moved to Brazil to work in factories.":"","People moved abroad to find new jobs and a better life.":"","When another city has good services, people want to move there.":"","For example, families want to live in a city with good hospitals and schools.":"","Suburbs are near the outside of a city.":"","Suburbs have more space for schools, hospitals, clinics, shopping malls, and zoos.":"","Some students go to universities in another country.":"","People often move to find new experiences and a better life.":"","If there are lots of sky lanterns in the sky, it's an amazing sight.":"","If someone finds a lantern, they sometimes get a secret message.":"","Is it exciting when there's a big fireworks display?":"","The following three poets come from two countries.":"","The river is gold.":"","However, the language they use is the same.":"","He enjoys writing poetry.":"","He and his daughter are eating.":"","A raisin has escaped from the raisin jar.":"","It is leaping in the air like a kangaroo.":"","His poem \"Colour\" encourages children to be creative.":"","She was an award-winning poet, writer, and playwright.":"","Do you like grasshoppers and beetles?":"","The crickets in the thickets.":"","Butterflies, ladybugs, and bees don't smell with little noses but with feelers.":"","I wonder how they sneeze.":"","I get up at night and dress by yellow candle-light.":"","Do you notice how winter days are short and summer days are long?":"","Hear the grown-up people's feet still going past me in the street.":"","And does it not seem hard to you?":"","Use the past continuous to talk about things that were happening at a certain time in the past.":"","Poets choose words carefully to help readers see a picture in their minds.":"","They want to share the beauty and joy of life.":"","A good poet observes things carefully.":"","Use each letter as the beginning of a new word.":"","They don't have to be rhyming words.":"","Her blond hair is glittering under the light.":"","Tiny snowflakes kiss my nose.":"","Write a sentence about the topic word.":"","Haiku poems use an exact number of syllables in each line.":"","When you describe something, you explain how it looks, sounds, or feels.":"","I was in the park when I saw some actors on a stage. They were performing a play when I saw them.":"","He tried to call the ambulance when his cell phone battery ran out.":"","Notice their labels and titles.":"","We learn how the movement of Earth helps us tell time.":"","The Earth turns, or spins, on an imaginary line called axis.":"","The time it takes for the Earth to make one complete turn is called a day.":"","A day is divided into hours, minutes, and seconds.":"","Multiply 24 hours by 60 minutes to get the answer.":"","The Earth travels around, or orbits, the sun.":"","The time it takes for the Earth to go around the sun once is called a year.":"","One year is equal to 12 months, or just over 52 weeks.":"","To be very accurate, it takes the Earth 365 days, 49 minutes, and 12 seconds to go around the sun.":"","Each time zone is one hour apart from the next time zone.":"","Thanks to clocks and calendars, we can measure time very easily.":"","It is the movement of the Earth that really allows us to measure time.":"","We will see the highest tides in the world there.":"","100 billion tons of water will move into the bay.":"","We'll hunt for fossils in the sand, and we will explore the caves.":"","What day will it be tomorrow?":"","The shadows will not be very long in the summer because the sun rises high in the sky in the summer.":"","A solution is how a character fixes the problem.":"","She packed for her business trip to Japan.":"","Molly stood beside her with a notebook and a pencil.":"","Do you have your passport, Mom?":"","Your destination is Tokyo.":"","You should be at the airport two hours early.":"","Remember passengers can only check two bags.":"","Please take good care of him while I'm gone.":"","I have a bad earache. I think I'm sick.":"","Mom put me in charge.":"","Tokyo is sixteen hours ahead of Los Angeles.":"","Molly's messages continued through the day.":"","Now Dad has a headache and a fever.":"","I also put a cold washcloth on his forehead.":"","Dad has a cold now. He's sneezing a lot. I gave him lots of tissues.":"","The doorbell didn't ring. The phone rang. Molly picked it up.":"","What are the announcements about?":"","They are not going to take a lot of luggage because they're going to carry their bags all the time.":"","The kite, the pinwheel, and the seeds are all moved by wind power.":"","Wind power is a source of energy.":"","Wind turns the blades on a windmill.":"","We can use wind power to make electricity.":"","Electricity powers lights and refrigerators.":"","Most of our energy comes from oil, natural gas, and coal. These energy sources are called fossil fuels.":"","Fossil fuels are made from the remains of things that lived millions of years ago.":"","A power plant burns coal to make electricity.":"","Wind power is a clean source of energy. It doesn't cause pollution. We will not run out of wind. It is a renewable resource.":"","Modern windmills called wind turbines make electricity.":"","The tall part is usually hollow and made of metal instead of wood.":"","Wind may be one important source of energy in the future.":"","Energy from water and the sun might also help reduce our need for fossil fuels.":"","A turbine looks different from the old type of windmill.":"","Electric car might be the answer to this problem.":"","One day, there may be more alternative energy to power electric cars, too.":"","Which sentence express certainty? Which express uncertainty?":"","Use may and might to talk about future possibility.":"","We will put solar panels on our roofs.":""});
